00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:04.969
For anyone who isn’t caught up on Flat Earth,
this discussion is motivated by the recent

00:02:04.969 --> 00:02:08.830
Netflix documentary: “Behind the Curve,”
but don’t worry, you don’t really need

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:09.800
to have watched it.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.340
Flat Earth theories are a little bit scattered
in their beliefs - is it a dome or an infinite

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.140
plane, how far away is the sun, what causes
an eclipse, etc. but they’re unified in

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:24.380
the idea that the Earth-as-sphere is deliberate
misinformation propagated by some shadow-y

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:29.011
agents, including but not limited to: Nasa,
the governments of the world, and probably

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.580
after this video, Wisecrack.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:35.160
One prominent model featured in Behind the
Curve is that the Earth is a flat plane, enclosed

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.860
in a dome called a “firmament,”

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:41.580
"Seventy percent of them believe that this is covered by some sort of dome"

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.360
A concept that dates back at least to the
Biblical story of Genesis.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.460
The sun travels in circles above the earth,
not millions of miles away, as understood

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.070
by scientists, but thousands.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.800
And It’s not really a huge ball of fire
radiating light in all directions, but along

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.460
with the moon, is more like a flashlight illuminating
part of the globe.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.160
So how does one get to the point where they
reject the round earth?

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.900
Well, you ask questions like: Why don’t
planes go to, or pass, Antarctica?

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.120
Why haven’t oil companies set up shop on
Antarctica?

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.940
Why are there only composite images of the
Earth, and not whole images?

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:19.040
Now your first thought might be: “These
people are complete idiots, why are you wasting

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.040
your time on this?”.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.960
But, Behind the Curve complicates this understanding.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.980
We see smart, critical humans who say things
like this,

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.280
“I became a Flat Earther cause I tried to
debunk Flat Earth”

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.060
or this,

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.260
“I mean I think that the scientific method
is the best way to get to the truth”

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.520
or a guy who is smart and talented enough
to make a badass motorcycle out of wood - which,

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.140
hey, I couldn’t do if I tried.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.720
Flat Earth and other debates about otherwise
accepted scientific fact bring out a much

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.200
larger problem: Our understanding of science
is terrible.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.360
And I’m not complaining that people don’t
remember the laws of thermodynamics or that

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.340
I still don’t understand how magnets work.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.980
“Water, fire, air and dirt, f**king magnets,
how do they work?”

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.180
I’m talking about the philosophy of science.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.820
So what is the philosophy of science?

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:07.960
It’s philosophy - obviously - that asks
questions like “how do we distinguish science

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:12.900
from non-science?” - and with that - how
should we weigh evidence when testing a hypothesis?

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.060
What kind of evidence is acceptable?

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:17.540
Basically, how do we know if we know shit?

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.079
You might remember learning the scientific
method, and that’s part of it, but it barely

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:22.729
scratches the surface.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:26.320
There are a lot of philosophies of science,
and I’m not here to tell you what the “right”

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.480
model is.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:31.590
It’s important to understand that all of
these frameworks have strengths and weaknesses.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:35.819
And to us, it’s our general ignorance of
how science works that allows for the abuse

00:04:35.819 --> 00:04:38.770
of scientific language we see in things like
Flat Earth.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:42.990
So to get a better understanding of how Flat
Earthers can use the language of science and

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:46.080
evidence to persuade people, let’s go back
in time.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:50.419
In the early 1900s, there was a scientific
doctrine posed by a group known as logical

00:04:50.419 --> 00:04:53.509
positivists called verificationism.

00:04:53.509 --> 00:04:57.530
This model essentially posits that science
is something that can be verified.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.129
If it can’t be verified - it ain’t science.

00:05:00.129 --> 00:05:04.580
So philosophical statements like “The meaning
of life is “be excellent to each other.”

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.840
- not science, because, you know, how would
you verify that?

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.699
Let’s start with a very simple example.

00:05:09.699 --> 00:05:14.289
If I were to say this swan is white, you could
say, hey, it looks white to me.

00:05:14.289 --> 00:05:17.950
I could pass it around and you could also
verify it is white.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:22.550
So- awesome, we’re using our senses in a
way that can be replicated by others - so

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:26.969
it’s been verified, and as such, “this
swan is white” could be considered a meaningful

00:05:26.969 --> 00:05:28.499
scientific statement.

00:05:28.499 --> 00:05:32.880
In this model, if you want to verify that
the Earth is round, or flat, one way would

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.020
be to go up in space and look at it.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.729
“How do you know it’s a globe, well it’s
because you saw this.

00:05:37.729 --> 00:05:41.260
It’s not like you’ve been up there in
your Jetsons car, nobody’s got a spaceship”

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:46.620
And in this way, Flat Earthers seem to at
least allude to this basic idea of verification.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:51.280
But how do you verify a statement like “All
swans are white,” which Europeans considered

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.440
to be the case before the 1600s.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.440
Let’s say you and others have encountered
thousands of swans, and every single one was

00:05:58.449 --> 00:05:59.449
white.

00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:00.889
Is this evidence enough?

00:06:00.889 --> 00:06:02.830
Well, not quite for the verificationist.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.460
And this was a huge problem for them.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:10.370
When it came to universal statements like
all swans are white, all Hipsters drink PBR,

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:14.199
all mass exerts gravitational pull - you can
never truly verify that.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:18.600
What if there’s a theoretical hipster out
there who shuns PBR in favor of Heineken?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.960
“Heineken?"

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.560
"F*ck that sh*t."

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.180
"Pabst Blue Ribbon!”

00:06:23.189 --> 00:06:24.930
Or, a black swan.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:29.460
Which - by the way - was discovered by Europeans
in Australia in the 1690s.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:33.999
Now, Flat Earthers may latch onto this logic
and say, well - we haven’t VERIFIED the

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.560
earth is round with our eyes.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:39.860
But if we try to apply this as a doctrine
for science, that all individuals have to

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.690
see things with our eyes, it’d be pretty
limiting.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:47.610
“If there’s uh, if there’s an event
like uh - I’ll just use Boston Bombing again

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:51.780
- I’m not going to believe any of those
events are real unless myself, I get my leg

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:52.500
blown off”

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:56.320
But, as far as our “all swans are white
problem,” this was a pretty big crisis for

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:01.820
verificationism, until a philosopher named
Karl Popper proposed a now-famous solution.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:07.100
Rather than focusing on verification, scientists
should rather focus on falsification.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:11.200
For Popper, good science is coming up with
a hypothesis, and then trying REALLY hard

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.140
to prove it wrong.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:17.139
If you can’t, you can be confident in your
hypothesis - say that all swans are white

00:07:17.139 --> 00:07:21.460
- but that doesn’t mean it won’t get proven
wrong when say, we discover a black swan or

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:22.800
two in ensuing decades.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.979
If a statement could not, theoretically be
falsified, it ain’t science.

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:31.330
So “The meaning of life is to be excellent
to each other”, is still not science.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:35.509
So if I thought the Earth was flat, I might
design several experiments which could prove

00:07:35.509 --> 00:07:36.880
it wasn’t flat.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:41.220
And if my hypothesis that “the earth isn’t
flat” is correct then it’s probably time

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:42.640
to abandon Flat Earth.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:47.940
Importantly, proving that the Earth is not
flat does not prove it is round, nor does

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.360
proving the Earth is not round prove it is
flat.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.240
What if it’s say, a doughnut balanced on
a giant turtle?

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.749
We’re going to talk a lot about Popper here,
but I should probably mention there are other

00:07:57.749 --> 00:07:58.749
approaches too.

00:07:58.749 --> 00:08:02.660
For instance, the probabilistic approach of
someone like Thomas Bayes, who would do some

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.970
math to give you a probability for something
to be true.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:10.369
So a statement like “I am 90% confident
that eating 5 tide pods will kill you.”

00:08:10.369 --> 00:08:13.900
And you might be wondering - are Flat Earthers
good falsificationists?

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:14.930
“We test everything”

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:18.380
You might say hey - they’re giving contrary
evidence - there’s an experiment in the

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:21.040
1800s , flight patterns, and our eyes.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.960
“Right out there, that’s Seattle.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:27.920
You shouldn’t be able to see it, there should
be hundreds of feet of curvature between us

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:28.540
and them.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.820
You should barely be able to see the tops
of those buildings”

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.740
But there’s a few problems, but let’s
focus on two.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:34.240
1.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.360
Their evidence is usually bad and 2.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:41.240
A big part of falsification is trying to prove
your own theory wrong, not proving someone

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.540
else wrong to prove yourself right.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:49.160
So for the first one, let’s look at a darling experiment for Flat Earthers, the Bedford Level Experiment.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:54.029
Samuel Rowbotham wanted to see if a boat would
actually dip below the horizon as it would

00:08:54.029 --> 00:08:54.820
on a globe.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.220
And it didn’t.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.620
So, round earth disproved?

00:08:58.620 --> 00:08:59.380
Not really.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:03.740
Experiment design in science is really hard,
one of the hardest things can be controlling

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:08.279
what are called confounding variables - ie:
external stuff that is going to screw up your

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:08.900
results.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:13.700
And for the Bedford Level Experiment, that
confounding variable was atmospheric refraction

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:16.579
- the bending of light caused by different
air densities.

00:09:16.579 --> 00:09:21.589
So, you design a new experiment to control
for that variable, and you can test that - which

00:09:21.589 --> 00:09:24.560
Alfred Russel Wallace - a famous scientist
- did.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:29.560
And that experiment, which uses objects that
are higher up to control for refraction, provided

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:31.340
evidence that the Earth was round.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:35.360
It’s also, more or less, the experiment
this guy does in the documentary.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:39.110
Which brings us to the second point, and an
actually interesting question for science

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:40.580
and falsificationism.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:44.580
Scientists raising contrary evidence is important
in the scientific community.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:49.860
But Flat Earthers don’t just want to falsify
the round Earth, they want to prove a Flat Earth.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:55.100
And that statement - that the earth is flat,
as Popper would argue, also needs to be tested.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:10:02.600
“We have constantly to criticize our own
fields, our own interpretations”

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:03.840
But... can it?

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:07.220
Let’s look at how this plays out with this
guy and his laser gyroscope, and this guy

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.220
with his flashlights.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:13.399
In the case of the gyroscope, a drifting gyroscope
would suggest that the Earth is not flat - which

00:10:13.399 --> 00:10:14.699
turns out to be the case.

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:18.700
“We found that we were picking up a drift.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.220
A 15° per hour drift”

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:26.420
And, with the flashlight experiment, a light
source that did not align with his holes correctly

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:30.440
would also suggest that the Earth is not flat,
which also happened.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.440
“Interesting.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.990
Interesting there”

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:38.019
So time to drop your previous hypothesis and
come up with a new one to falsify.

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:38.680
Right?

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:39.680
Well, not quite.

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:43.920
The problem with most woo-woo, whether that’s
anti-vaxxers, Flat Earthers, creationists,

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:48.800
and so on, is that if you ask them, “What
evidence would you require to renounce this

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.700
theory,” the answer is: it probably doesn’t
exist.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.800
“I won’t change my mind on anything!

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:56.620
Regardless of the facts that are set out before
me”

00:10:56.620 --> 00:11:01.000
As Behind the Curve highlights, even evidence
to the contrary isn’t quite enough.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:05.480
Instead of moving on, Laser gyroscope guy
is convinced that heavenly energies are messing

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:10.190
with his data, and the flashlight guy had…
some kind of reason to ignore the results

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.269
of his experiment.

00:11:11.269 --> 00:11:15.060
“Proposing a theory that can be falsified”
doesn’t seem to be the name of the game

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.060
for woo-woo.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:20.420
This point is made so ironically clear when
Patricia Steere, a Flat Earther, realizes

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:26.079
that claims that she works for the CIA can never
be sufficiently disproven to satisfy her critics.

00:11:26.079 --> 00:11:32.050
“The thing about all of these things, is
I can’t prove any of it...wrong”

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:36.130
Believe it or not, this kind of mental gymnastics
that we see with our Flat Earth experimenters

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:40.120
is a basic problem in a ton of science - not
just Flat Earthers.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:46.139
Because one compelling criticism of falsificationism
is that tests and hypotheses don’t exist

00:11:46.139 --> 00:11:49.860
in vacuums, they exist in larger systematized
theories.

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:55.089
If we consider science to be simply the process
of trying to falsify various claims, we can

00:11:55.089 --> 00:11:59.860
see the limits of this model with Newton’s
physics, who I think we could all agree is

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.360
an OG scientist.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:06.060
Newton came up with his laws of motion, his
theory of gravity - he also invented calculus.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:07.640
And they all worked together.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:11.680
Armed with Newton’s theories, scientists
made predictions about how the solar system

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:16.200
worked, figuring out celestial orbits with
a combination of observation and math.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:20.639
Building on his theories, scientists made
new claims, and tested those claims.

00:12:20.639 --> 00:12:23.779
And then those claims would become the bases
for other tests.

00:12:23.779 --> 00:12:24.779
“Yeah Science!”

00:12:24.779 --> 00:12:26.670
Now, where’s the problem?

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:31.670
Well, Newton’s model predicted Mercury’s
orbit would do one thing, and then it did…

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:32.520
not that.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:37.900
So does this falsify Newton’s model, and
if so, should we all just drop it and move

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:38.400
on?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:42.500
"Course, he also thought he could turn
metal into gold and died eating mercury - making

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.640
him yet another stupid -

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.060
-bitch!”

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:50.970
Well, in contrasts to falsificationism, physicist
Thomas Kuhn understands science as working

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:51.970
in paradigms.

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:56.149
So, for Newton’s physics, keep on poking
holes in it, but don’t throw the baby out

00:12:56.149 --> 00:13:00.660
with the bathwater until your inquiries point
to some bigger badder paradigm that comes

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:05.640
around and can do everything Newton’s model
can do - but better - in this case, that bigger

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.580
badder paradigm was Einstein’s relativity.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:13.480
And, so for Newton, instead of Mercury proving
him wrong, scientists just tweaked the model

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:15.170
for as long as they could.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:19.839
Newton’s law could accurately predict so
much - not just the movement of most celestial

00:13:19.839 --> 00:13:23.870
bodies, but basic locomotion, engineering,
and so much more.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:27.000
So certainly it wouldn’t be good to throw
it all away?

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:30.800
To address this issue, some people just said,
hey, there’s another planet that would make

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:34.220
Mercury’s orbit weird, and Newton is still
right!

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:35.400
System tweaked.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:39.480
And in a perverse way, this is kind of how
Flat Earthers operate.

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:44.560
While you might say “The gyroscope drifted,
Flat Earthers owned” in reality, they just

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:48.600
tweak the model, in this case, by positing
the existence of heavenly energies.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.900
But does that make Flat Earthers real scientists?

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:53.460
Unfortunately, no.

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:56.959
Because these “tweaks” should also get
subjected to experiments.

00:13:57.180 --> 00:14:01.320
So, if you’re going to say heavenly energies
are a confounding variable for your gyroscope

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.520
experiment, you better find evidence of heavenly
energies.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:08.960
And if you can’t find any, maybe you should
ask, is my model wrong?

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:13.040
Maybe I should test a new hypothesis: that
the Earth is round.

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:16.579
According to Thomas Kuhn - this is how science
works.

00:14:16.579 --> 00:14:20.639
You have scientists working off a bunch of
unquestioned assumptions - that gravity works

00:14:20.639 --> 00:14:25.680
like this, motion works like this - and then
contrary evidence starts piling up.

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:29.839
The system isn’t overturned until someone
comes along and suggests a new foundation

00:14:29.839 --> 00:14:33.779
to work off of, and then scientists kind of
duke it out over who is right.

00:14:33.779 --> 00:14:38.110
Einstein’s model, for instance, could account
for Mercury’s weird orbit, and a bunch of

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.870
other stuff, while being able to make all
the good predictions that Newton’s model

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:43.060
already did.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:45.730
Kuhn calls this a paradigm shift.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:50.300
Progress in science is built on people arguing
over the truth before a new paradigm becomes

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:53.980
the consensus - not necessarily Capital T
truths.

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:58.220
Ok - so are Flat Earther’s the Einsteins
in this story, pointing to contrary evidence

00:14:58.230 --> 00:14:59.959
for a full paradigm shift?

00:14:59.959 --> 00:15:03.360
“We’re not just winning, we’re crushing
them”

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:04.100
Well not quite.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:05.639
“I don’t know how people believe that”

00:15:05.639 --> 00:15:09.120
You can think of Einstein coming along and
saying, “My model can do everything that

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:12.120
yours can do - but better!” - because it
did.

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:17.160
Can the Flat Earth model help build long bridges,
a functioning global positioning system, navigate

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:21.851
airplanes, launch missiles across the continents,
transmit TV to your house via satellite, or

00:15:21.851 --> 00:15:27.009
do literally any of the hundreds if not thousands
of things that are predicated on a round Earth?

00:15:27.009 --> 00:15:27.700
Nope.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:32.000
And yet, they still persist, which brings
us to something a little outside the realm

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:36.020
of science and into a pressing problem for
the modern world: JAQing off.

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:41.200
YouTube overlords, please don’t demonetize
this, because we’re talking about Just Asking

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.780
Questions - ing off.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:47.220
It is an epidemic in almost every modern political
or internet debate.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:48.220
It goes like this:

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:50.440
“Is Wendy using your lunch money to buy
Heroine?

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:51.380
Probably not.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:52.400
But how can we know?

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:54.340
I don’t want my lunch money going to drugs!

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:55.660
Who’s taking these drugs?

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:56.540
What would be the point?

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:57.340
I’m asking questions!”

00:15:57.340 --> 00:16:01.660
In the case of Mark Sargent’s massively
popular “Flat Earth clues,” it's one

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:02.880
big circle JAQ.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:07.500
While it may take 5-seconds to raise the question,
“Why aren’t oil companies drilling in

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:12.140
Antarctica,” it could take you a good 5
minutes to learn that in 1959, scientists

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:15.779
convinced a bunch of countries that they shouldn’t
bring all their bullsh*t to the most remote

00:16:15.779 --> 00:16:17.250
and wild place on Earth.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:20.720
A few minutes later, you might learn these
scientists argued that Antarctica should be

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:23.660
open to discovery for people all over the
world.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:28.180
In five more minutes, you might also learn
that, in 1991, to clarify things, they signed

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:32.839
another treaty explicitly stating that, to
preserve Antarctica's environment, there can

00:16:32.839 --> 00:16:35.490
be no commercial activity for 50 years.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:40.180
Also, as it turns out, extracting stuff from
the most remote place on earth is extremely

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.560
expensive, and kind of dangerous.

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:47.370
The original question - why don’t companies
drill in Antarctica, is like arguing a national

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:51.760
park doesn’t exist because - obviously,
oil companies would be all up on that if it

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:52.260
did.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:55.920
And look, that took me all that time to answer
one single question.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:59.980
Another great example is flight patterns,
where a Flat Earther might ask questions like

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.759
“WHY DIDN’T THEY GO HERE,” in which
case you would have to explain how projecting

00:17:03.759 --> 00:17:08.069
a sphere onto a flat image distorts images,
which was a cool thing we learned when we

00:17:08.069 --> 00:17:12.340
all discovered that Greenland is not as big
as Africa . So why didn’t they go this other

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:12.940
way?

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:17.060
Because it would take longer, or there’s
not enough demand for a direct flight.

00:17:17.079 --> 00:17:20.260
Flat Earthers may say they’re “winning
the debate” against round earthers, but

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:24.079
this is more a statement on how profoundly
bad public debates can be.

00:17:24.079 --> 00:17:29.610
If, in science, the burden of proof rests
on you to prove your hypothesis, JAQing off

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:34.400
functions by dumping the burden of proof on
you with about 8 million questions.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:37.500
And by the time I’ve answered your question
about “why aren’t there flights over the

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:41.400
South Pole,” you’re ready to raise 5 more
“simple questions.”

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:44.220
How do we reconcile this with the fact that,
like this guy,

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.000
science is built on asking questions?

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:56.820
One of the primary problems is that questions
aren’t meant to exclusively start a debate.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:59.180
It’s not I win and you lose.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:04.500
Rather, questions seek to start conversations
that build consensus, like saying “Hey,

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:08.040
Mercury is doing some weird shit over here,”
let’s all figure this out.

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:12.320
Instead, the questions posed by Flat Earthers
are meant to “prove” the Earth is flat

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.789
by drawing doubt on the round Earth.

00:18:14.789 --> 00:18:18.460
These kinds of arguments can be appealing
because, on the surface, leaving questions

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:21.960
unanswered looks like you’re wrong, or hiding something.

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:26.230
So instead of dumping on Flat Earthers, it’s
important for us to understand how science

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:31.400
is done, how scientific consensus is made,
and even be critical of when science is done

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:32.040
badly.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:36.720
For instance, there’s a ton of psychology
studies out there that can’t be replicated.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:40.400
And that is bad science, but it’s probably
not a conspiracy.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:43.300
Alright, there is one more thing worth answering.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:44.300
Why?

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:45.890
Why are Flat Earthers a thing?

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:50.170
There are a lot of ways to account for Flat
Earthers and other conspiracy theories.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:53.890
Some psychologists have suggested that conspiracy theories appeal to people who either feel

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:58.539
powerless or insignificant in society . And
yeah, we get that.

00:18:58.539 --> 00:19:02.741
In a world where literally everything is outside of your control, cracking the “real” answer

00:19:02.741 --> 00:19:04.720
to who shot JFK is appealing.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:08.380
It can make it feel like the world is rational
and predictable.

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:11.130
And that seems to be the basic appeal of Flat Earth.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:16.090
That we’re not a tiny blue marble drifting
in the cosmos, but a special little terrarium

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:17.640
that’s the center of the universe.

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:19.440
But unfortunately for this lady,

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:27.760
science isn’t about putting together random facts like pieces of a puzzle.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:31.880
Flat Earthers speak to a larger crisis of
trust going on in our society.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:36.559
And rather than relegating it to some corner of the internet with Chuck E Cheese truthers,

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:41.080
we should understand it as a larger crisis
of the erosion of faith in expertise of all

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:41.680
kinds.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:45.020
And this isn’t harmless as we can see with
this guy.

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:52.070
“They want people dumb, blind, deaf to the
truth, so they can inject you with their vaccines

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:54.280
and their public schooling”

00:19:54.280 --> 00:19:58.820
It’s not just that we need more scientists
to understand genetics and evolution to cure

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:04.300
disease, but that this line of conspiratorial
thinking can make almost anything possible,

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:08.100
from claiming a woman named Patricia works for the CIA because of the last 3 letters

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:12.300
of her name, to sending death threats to people who you think are crisis actors.

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:16.780
And that’s not even to talk about the almost
extinct diseases that are making a comeback

00:20:16.789 --> 00:20:18.029
and killing people.

00:20:18.029 --> 00:20:19.029
Thanks, internet.

00:20:19.029 --> 00:20:23.640
It’s not that we should have blind faith
in the talking heads of science, but understand

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:26.880
the conventions and practices that got them to their conclusion.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:29.160
Was their experiment designed well?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:32.280
What level of confidence do they ascribe to
their predictions?

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:38.240
Does contrary evidence debunk a model, or
is it inevitable when studying things as complicated

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.910
as, say, quantum physics or climate.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:42.050
So - what do you think?

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:47.200
Do we need better education on how science works, or am I collecting my check from NASA?

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:48.640
Well, It’s actually Wix.

00:20:48.649 --> 00:20:52.190
You can build your own website for free by
clicking the link in the description, and

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:55.060
as always, thanks for watching guys, peace.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.920
Peace.

